    "contents" : "---\ntitle: \"NHTSA DSFS Meta-Analysis\"\nauthor: \"Dan Flynn\"\ndate: \"September 27, 2016\"\noutput: pdf_document\n---\n\n```{r setup, include=FALSE}\nknitr::opts_chunk$set(echo = FALSE)\n\nsetwd(\"~/git/dsfs\")\n\nsource(\"MA_Analysis_Prep.R\")\n```\n\n### Background\n\nQuantitative meta-analysis of the effectiveness of Dynamic Speed Feedback Signs (DSFS) in reducing driving speeds.\n\nHypotheses:\n\nHypothesis        | Calculation    \n------------------|------------------------------------------------------------\nH1A. Activation   | (Upstream - Adjacent)_Before - (Upstream - Adjacent)_During\nH1B. Activation   | Before - During\nH2A. Deactivation | (Upstream - Adjacent)_During - (Upstream - Adjacent)_After\nH2B. Deactivation | During - After\n\n\n\nArticles were located from searches the databases TRID, National Transportation Library (NTL), WorldShare, Academic Search Complete, PsycINFO, Web of Science, and Science Direct. The searches were done between 3/9/2016 and 3/16/2016.  Any of the search terms in the tables that ended in 's' were wildcards with *.\n\n## Activation hypothesis\n\n```{r, echo=FALSE}\n\n\n```\n\n\n",
